{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779125340,"nonce":"zoyJuJc/JKnB8RoHnvPSItAFHBM=","message":"## Cross-Reference: sweeps/protocols/metrics must be authored, not table metadata\n\nThe Train/Evaluate collection UI review on `f0ae3ce` clarified an important structural-authoring requirement.\n\nThe bottom pane should not imply that sweeps, protocols, task variants, loss terms, metrics, or descriptive run text appear magically as metadata. These need to originate from editable scenario/task/objective/protocol specs, mostly authored in the top structural workspace and its inspectors:\n\n- Sweep variants should come from explicit user choices over task parameters, objective/loss parameters, seeds/replicates, training protocol fields, or named templates.\n- Run labels should be deterministic summaries of those authored choices, with optional user rename support.\n- Evaluation protocols should be editable/inheritable scenario/protocol state, not a static descriptive card.\n- Training metrics shown in run tables should come from metric/objective/analysis specs or task templates, not hardcoded columns. See `e5a1e6c`.\n- Loss/objective authoring belongs in this structural workspace; optimizer/batches/checkpoint cadence/compute target belong in a concise training protocol editor tied to the stage.\n\nThis reinforces the existing acceptance criteria here: top-pane edits to task, loss/objective, probes, temporal selectors, and metrics must persist as typed specs and lower to executable Feedbax state.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}